Subject: A recovery added a passkey to your account

--- text/plain ---
Hello,

A recovery added a passkey to your account.

Someone used a recovery link from SourceOrigin support to add a passkey and sign in. Until the recovery settles, that passkey can sign in but can’t change your account’s security settings. If it wasn’t you, undo the recovery with a passkey from before it: that removes the new passkey, signs every device out and withdraws every app’s access. With no passkey from before it, contact SourceOrigin support, who can undo it for you.

Undo the recovery:

https://auth.sourceorigin.dev/recover/undo#recovery=RECOVERY

Read it in your Origin Account notifications.

https://auth.sourceorigin.dev/settings/notifications/NOTIFICATION

If this wasn’t you and you can’t sign in to secure your account, sign it out of every device and app, without signing in. The link works once, for 7 days.

https://auth.sourceorigin.dev/sign-out#token=TOKEN

SourceOrigin

