<p>Hello,</p>
<p>
<strong>A recovery added a passkey to your account.</strong>
</p>
<p>Someone used a recovery link from SourceOrigin support to add a passkey and sign in. Until the recovery settles, that passkey can sign in but can’t change your account’s security settings. If it wasn’t you, undo the recovery with a passkey from before it: that removes the new passkey, signs every device out and withdraws every app’s access. With no passkey from before it, contact SourceOrigin support, who can undo it for you.</p>
<p>
<a href="https://auth.sourceorigin.dev/recover/undo#recovery=RECOVERY" style="display:inline-block;padding:10px 18px;border-radius:8px;background:#1a1a1a;color:#ffffff;text-decoration:none">Undo the recovery</a>
</p>
<p style="font-size:14px;color:#555555">Or copy this link: https://auth.sourceorigin.dev/recover/undo#recovery=RECOVERY</p>
<p>Read it in <a href="https://auth.sourceorigin.dev/settings/notifications/NOTIFICATION">your Origin Account notifications</a>.</p>
<p style="font-size:14px;color:#555555">If this wasn’t you and you can’t sign in to secure your account, <a href="https://auth.sourceorigin.dev/sign-out#token=TOKEN">sign it out of every device and app</a>, without signing in. The link works once, for 7 days.</p>
<p>SourceOrigin</p>
</div>
